From: Tiago Damascena <tiagobdamascena@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Sep 2026 16:30:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: rk817_charger: pick the boot state of charge by what happened while off

Resolving the boot state of charge from the columb counter assumes the
counter keeps counting faithfully while the system is off. On an R36S
(RK3326, rk817) it does not: powered off without a cable it loses a
steady 175-200 mA-equivalent per hour -- 1872 mAh over 11 h, 602 mAh
over 3 h, proportional to OFF_CNT -- while the rested voltage at the
next power-on is unchanged (4.038 V both days). Taken at its word, a
cell at 99% booted as 36%, then as 16%. Powered off on the charger the
counter does see the charge, short by the same bias (+568 mAh counted
in an hour that delivered more).

PWRON_VOL, on the other hand, is sampled before the SoC draws anything:
4.038 V at power-on against 3.97 V under load 8 s later, on every boot
observed. It is the rested voltage the original driver looked up after
30 minutes off, and that lookup was right on this board.

So choose by what happened while off. Off less than 30 minutes (OFF_CNT
counts tens of minutes): the counter, which is continuous across a
short power cycle (95% -> 95%). Off longer and not charging at
power-on: the ocv lookup of PWRON_VOL, when it is inside the pack's
design range. Off longer and charging at power-on, where PWRON_VOL
reads under charge current (4.19 V measured) and the saved soc predates
the charge: the larger of the saved soc and the counter, which errs
low; the next rested pair corrects it upwards. A counter reading zero
or negative keeps the saved soc in every branch.

Extend the boot log line with the boot voltage, OFF_CNT, the current
and the source chosen, so the branch can be read from the log.

Measured on an R36S, 6.12.91 with the ROCKNIX rk817 series applied.

Signed-off-by: Tiago Damascena <tiagobdamascena@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/power/supply/rk817_charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/rk817_charger.c
@@ -877,6 +877,8 @@
 				struct power_supply_battery_info *bat_info)
 {
 	struct rk808 *rk808 = charger->rk808;
+	int off_time, cur_ua, raw_boot_uv, counter_soc, ocv_soc, saved_soc;
+	const char *source;
 	u32 boot_charge_mah;
 	int ret, reg, tmp;
 	bool first_boot;
@@ -928,30 +930,79 @@
 
 		/*
 		 * The columb counter keeps counting while the system is off,
-		 * so take it, capped at full, unless it reads invalid; the
-		 * saved soc is then at most one update interval old. A counter
-		 * that is merely wrong is corrected by the next rested relax
-		 * pair.
+		 * but not faithfully on every board. On an R36S it loses a
+		 * steady 175-200 mA-equivalent for every hour off (measured
+		 * over 3 h and 11 h, the rested voltage unchanged), so after a
+		 * long time off it reads far too low -- while it does see a
+		 * charge that happened powered off (+568 mAh in an hour on the
+		 * charger, less than went in). Pick the source by what happened
+		 * while off:
+		 *
+		 *  - off less than 30 minutes (OFF_CNT counts tens of minutes):
+		 *    the counter, continuous across a short power cycle;
+		 *  - off longer and not charging now: PWRON_VOL, sampled before
+		 *    the SoC draws anything and so a rested voltage (4.038 V
+		 *    against 3.97 V under load 8 s later, two days running):
+		 *    the ocv lookup the original driver used here;
+		 *  - off longer and charging now: PWRON_VOL reads under charge
+		 *    current and the saved soc predates the charge, but the
+		 *    counter saw at least part of it. The larger of the saved
+		 *    soc and the counter, which errs low; the next rested pair
+		 *    corrects it upwards.
+		 *
+		 * A counter that reads zero or negative is invalid in every
+		 * branch and leaves the saved soc.
 		 */
 		regmap_bulk_read(rk808->regmap, RK817_GAS_GAUGE_Q_PRES_H3,
 				 bulk_reg, 4);
 		tmp = get_unaligned_be32(bulk_reg);
-		dev_info(charger->dev,
-			 "boot: counter %d uAh, saved soc %d, fcc %d mAh, battery %d uV\n",
-			 tmp > 0 ? ADC_TO_CHARGE_UAH(tmp, charger->res_div) : 0,
-			 charger->soc, charger->fcc_mah,
-			 rk817_bat_voltage_uv(charger, RK817_GAS_GAUGE_BAT_VOL_H));
+		regmap_read(rk808->regmap, RK817_GAS_GAUGE_OFF_CNT, &off_time);
+		cur_ua = rk817_bat_current_ua(charger);
+		raw_boot_uv = rk817_bat_voltage_uv(charger,
+						   RK817_GAS_GAUGE_PWRON_VOL_H);
+
+		saved_soc = charger->soc;
+		counter_soc = -1;
 		if (tmp > 0) {
 			boot_charge_mah = ADC_TO_CHARGE_UAH(tmp,
 							    charger->res_div) / 1000;
 			if (boot_charge_mah > charger->fcc_mah)
 				boot_charge_mah = charger->fcc_mah;
-			charger->soc = boot_charge_mah * 100000 /
-				       charger->fcc_mah;
+			counter_soc = boot_charge_mah * 100000 /
+				      charger->fcc_mah;
+		}
+
+		if (off_time < 3) {
+			if (counter_soc >= 0) {
+				charger->soc = counter_soc;
+				source = "counter";
+			} else {
+				source = "saved soc (counter invalid)";
+			}
+		} else if (cur_ua <= 0 &&
+			   raw_boot_uv >= bat_info->voltage_min_design_uv &&
+			   raw_boot_uv <= bat_info->voltage_max_design_uv) {
+			ocv_soc = power_supply_batinfo_ocv2cap(bat_info,
+							       raw_boot_uv, 20);
+			if (ocv_soc >= 0) {
+				charger->soc = ocv_soc * 1000;
+				source = "rested boot voltage";
+			} else {
+				source = "saved soc (ocv lookup failed)";
+			}
+		} else if (counter_soc > charger->soc) {
+			charger->soc = counter_soc;
+			source = "counter (charging, above saved soc)";
 		} else {
-			dev_info(charger->dev,
-				 "columb counter invalid, keeping saved soc\n");
+			source = "saved soc";
 		}
+
+		dev_info(charger->dev,
+			 "boot: counter %d uAh, saved soc %d, fcc %d mAh, battery %d uV, boot %d uV, off %d, current %d uA: %s -> soc %d\n",
+			 tmp > 0 ? ADC_TO_CHARGE_UAH(tmp, charger->res_div) : 0,
+			 saved_soc, charger->fcc_mah,
+			 rk817_bat_voltage_uv(charger, RK817_GAS_GAUGE_BAT_VOL_H),
+			 raw_boot_uv, off_time, cur_ua, source, charger->soc);
 	}
 
 	/*
